<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE refentry PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook V4.1.2//EN"
  "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.1.2/docbookx.dtd">

<!-- $Id$ -->

<refentry id="gfarm-pcp.1">

<refentryinfo><date>10 Nov 2026</date></refentryinfo>

<refmeta>
<refentrytitle>gfarm-pcp</refentrytitle>
<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
<refmiscinfo>Gfarm</refmiscinfo>
</refmeta>

<refnamediv id="name">
<refname>gfarm-pcp</refname>
<refpurpose>copy files to multiple hosts</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv id="synopsis">
<cmdsynopsis sepchar=" ">
  <command moreinfo="none">gfarm-pcp</command>
    <arg choice="opt" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>options</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="plain" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>source</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="plain" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>destination</replaceable></arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
<cmdsynopsis sepchar=" ">
  <command moreinfo="none">gfarm-pcp</command>
    <arg choice="opt" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>options</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="plain" rep="repeat"><replaceable>source</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="plain" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>directory</replaceable></arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<!-- body begins here -->

<refsect1 id="description"><title>DESCRIPTION</title>
<para><command moreinfo="none">gfarm-pcp</command> copies local files
<parameter moreinfo="none">source</parameter> to
<parameter moreinfo="none">destination</parameter> or
<parameter moreinfo="none">directory</parameter> on each host listed in
a hostfile, by using a remote copy command,
<command moreinfo="none">scp -pr</command> by default.
A relative path of the destination is relative to the home directory
on the remote host.
It is useful, for example, to distribute configuration files to
filesystem nodes of Gfarm.</para>

<para>By default, files are copied to one host after another.
When the -p option is specified, files are copied to multiple hosts in
parallel.</para>

<para>The format of the hostfile, and how the local host is skipped,
are the same as <command moreinfo="none">gfarm-prun</command>.
See <citerefentry><refentrytitle>gfarm-prun</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>

<para>When the PRUN_RCP environment variable is set to
<literal>no</literal>, files are copied by the remote shell command
specified by the PRUN_RSH environment variable, without a remote copy
command.  In this case, the last argument must be a directory on the
remote host, and only regular files can be copied.
The permission of the files is not preserved.</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="options"><title>OPTIONS</title>
<variablelist>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-a</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Copies files also to the local host, if it is listed in the
hostfile.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-h</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">hostfile</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a hostfile.  If `-' is specified, the list of hosts is
read from the standard input.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-m</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">max_jobs</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies the maximum number of hosts to which files are copied
in parallel with the -p option.  The default is 16.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-n</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Displays the commands that would be executed, but does not
execute them.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-p</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Copies files to multiple hosts in parallel in the
background.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-rcp</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">rcp_command</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a remote copy command.  The default is
<command moreinfo="none">scp -pr</command>.  If <literal>no</literal>
is specified, files are copied by the remote shell command as
described above.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-v</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Displays the host name before copying files to the host.
This option has no effect with the -p option.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="environment-variables"><title>ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES</title>
<variablelist>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_RCP</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a remote copy command.  The default is
<command moreinfo="none">scp -pr</command>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_RSH</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a remote shell command that is used when PRUN_RCP is
<literal>no</literal>.  The default is
<command moreinfo="none">ssh</command>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_HOSTFILE</envar>, <envar>PRUN_HOSTNAME</envar>,
<envar>PRUN_MAX_JOBS</envar>, <envar>PRUN_PARALLEL</envar>,
<envar>PRUN_ALL_INCLUDE_MYSELF</envar>, <envar>PRUN_VERBOSE</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>The same as <command moreinfo="none">gfarm-prun</command>.
See <citerefentry><refentrytitle>gfarm-prun</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="exit-status"><title>EXIT STATUS</title>
<para><command moreinfo="none">gfarm-pcp</command> exits with 0 when
files are copied to all hosts successfully.  Otherwise, it exits with
the exit status of the copy command for a host to which the copy
fails.  When it fails for two or more hosts, the exit status for one
of them is returned.</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="examples"><title>EXAMPLES</title>
<para>Copies <filename moreinfo="none">gfarm2.conf</filename> to
<filename moreinfo="none">/tmp</filename> on all hosts listed in
<filename moreinfo="none">$HOME/.nodelist</filename>,
except the local host.</para>
<literallayout format="linespecific" class="normal">
	$ gfarm-pcp gfarm2.conf /tmp
</literallayout>

<para>Copies the shared secret key of the user to the home directory
on all hosts listed in <filename moreinfo="none">hosts</filename>, in
parallel.</para>
<literallayout format="linespecific" class="normal">
	$ gfarm-pcp -p -h hosts .gfarm_shared_key .
</literallayout>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="files"><title>FILES</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><filename moreinfo="none">$HOME/.nodelist</filename></term>
<listitem>
<para>the default hostfile</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="see-also"><title>SEE ALSO</title>
<para>
  <citerefentry>
  <refentrytitle>gfarm-prun</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
  </citerefentry>,
  <citerefentry>
  <refentrytitle>scp</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
  </citerefentry>
</para>
</refsect1>

</refentry>
